  "pre_synthesized_answer": "In rabbits, GALT is a central early-life site for postnatal B-cell repertoire diversification and selection, driven by microbiota-dependent expansion, somatic hypermutation, and gene conversion-like diversification; later, rabbits also undergo conventional antigen-driven affinity maturation.",
  "logic_list": [
    {
      "reasoning_type": "deductive",
      "logic": "Because the answer states rabbit B cells begin with a limited bone-marrow repertoire and then diversify in GALT through SHM and gene conversion, it concludes that GALT is a major site of primary repertoire building."
